Dummy Table AM
==============

Dummy table AM is a module for testing any facility usable by a table access
method.  The routine is a copy of the heap one with a few callbacks replaced,
so that a table created with this access method has real storage while the
answers the core gets from the AM are easy to predict.

Currently it only overrides relation_size(), which reports half of the heap
footprint for the main fork.  The number tracks the relation's real size but
is never equal to it, so the SQL-level size functions can be told apart from
plain file measurement, while RelationGetNumberOfBlocks() still stays within
the relation.
